          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mild bilateral conjunctival injection and profuse tearing; pupils 4–5 mm, equal and reactive; no miosis, ciliary flush, corneal opacity, foreign body seen on gross exam including lid eversion, eyelid oedema, purulent discharge, or photophobia. Visual acuity approximately 6/9 OU, uncorrected. Extraocular movements full and non-painful."
      }
